# V. Risk factors

# 1. AI Subversive Risk
Large language models and AI Agent may reduce the complexity of ERP implementation and customization and fundamentally weaken SAP ' s conversion costs for the mound. If AI allows businesses to integrate different systems more easily, SAP ' s core values are weakened.

#2. Cloud backlog growth decelerates
2026 The year-round cloud backlog growth guideline has been reduced from 25% to "slightly slowed" and, if this is trendy rather than temporary, will seriously affect the visibility of future income growth. Management attributes it to delays caused by the larger size of client projects, but this explanation needs to be validated.

#3. Oracle Competition
Oracle has already levelled SAP on its annual income, and Oracle has a unique advantage in databases and cloud infrastructure. If Oracle continues to win shares in the cloud ERP market, SAP growth will be under pressure.

##4. Currency risk
SAP reports in euros, but the bulk of the income is from the dollar area. Exchange rate fluctuations have a significant impact on the presentation, with 11 per cent of the increase in the fixed exchange rate in 2025, compared with 8 per cent in real terms.

##5. Client migration implementation risks
The relocation of hundreds of thousands of business clients from local deployment to cloudy ends is a complex project.

